  "question": {
    "text": "A galvanometer of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi></math> is converted into a voltameter of range <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> by connecting a resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> in series with it. The additional resistance that should be connected in series with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> to increase the range of the voltmeter to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> will be :"
  },
